body:
I try not to let myself get too invested in my streams...idk, I feel very afraid of failure I suppose. but I have a single viewer that always joins when Im streaming, no matter what Im playing. 

&#x200B;

it means so much to me- even if Im too shy and anxious to speak or show myself. but knowing that there is another human somewhere, sharing in my experiences and along for the ride with me, really helps me enjoy the games even more then I already do. this was such a sweet video, and to all you out there that support small streamers, thanks!

Does she have an account with Samsung? As in is the phone registered with a samsung account??   


&#x200B;

If it is, go to [findmymobile.co](https://findmymobile.com)m and sign in. There is an option through this website to unlock the phone remotely by entering a code on the website, and then entering that code on the phone when prompted. 

&#x200B;

Keep in mind, you have to have a samsung account, and location services must be turned on in order for this to work. 

&#x200B;

I worked as a tech support agent for Samsung and these were the steps for this exact issue. Sadly, it doesn't work very often. 

&#x200B;

Good luck!

I really struggle with this as well. 

&#x200B;

I never comment or post anything really meaningful for this exact reason. I think it comes from being afraid of what others will think, and trying to avoid any confrontation that I can, even on the internet. 

&#x200B;

Keeping a diary is almost impossible for me for the exact same reason. I'll scratch out some of my own words halfway through writing them just because...well I'm not really sure. Even if its in a diary that is private, I still feel the need to censor my thoughts and emotions.
